        "content": "A practical order of operations for the weekly plan: first place recurring maintenance on its regular days. Then look at the pending installs and assign them by priority (promised dates, deposits received, material on hand). Then fill gaps with smaller one-time jobs and enhancements near routes that are already running. Finally, leave some slack. A crew scheduled at 100 percent on Monday will be behind by Wednesday.\n\nCheck materials before you lock in an install date. Nothing wastes a crew day like showing up to a sod job when the sod delivery is tomorrow. Many companies confirm material orders as part of the Thursday planning for the following week. For maintenance, the post on [routing maintenance crews](/blog/landscaping/landscaping-route-optimization-software) goes into how to group stops so the days are actually achievable."
