        "content": "Commercial bids usually come with a specification: mowing frequency, height, trimming and edging requirements, bed maintenance standards, pruning schedules, seasonal color rotations, irrigation checks, leaf removal, and sometimes snow. Read every line. The spec is what you will be held to, and the cheapest bid usually wins by quietly ignoring part of it.\n\nWalk the property with the spec in hand. Measure turf and bed areas (a satellite measure map gets you most of the way on big sites), count the trees and shrubs that need pruning, note the slopes, retention ponds and obstacles that slow mowing. Then price each item in the spec separately, so you can show the manager exactly what they are getting and defend the number if a competitor comes in lower."
